WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.670
London, 1794.

2
00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:03.580
Night.

3
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:09.410
A man walks the streets: "I wander thro'
each charter'd street," In every face

4
00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:13.740
he meets, he sees marks of
weakness, and marks of woe.

5
00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:15.600
And he hears it everywhere.

6
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:16.910
A man's cry.

7
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.490
A baby's fear.

8
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.760
A chimney sweep.

9
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.350
A soldier's sigh.

10
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.610
Every voice is miserable.

11
00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:25.200
So whose fault is it?

12
00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:29.190
In this mission, you'll find out what
charter'd means in William Blake's Songs

13
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.440
of Experience.

14
00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:34.450
You'll count how often one
small word repeats: every.

15
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.960
And you'll walk past
a church and a palace,

16
00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:39.550
and see what Blake places beside them.

17
00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:42.370
Your mission: decide whose fault it is.
